I tend to encounter more rats than seems normal with this role,
actually.  I don't know if it's a coincidence, but I had wondered that
since rats tend to be generated in small groups, and the game
generates a rat as your starting pet, if as a side effect it may
sometimes create other rats at the same time at the beginning of the
game?

Anyway, that aside, I rather like the idea of adding more flavor to
the role by making rats peaceful or tamable.  I am concerned that
making them both peaceful AND tamable would be too easy, though, being
able to freely wander among the peaceful rat hordes and make tons of
pets.

Still, I really do like both ideas, and want to think of a way to
implement them in a balanced way.  Anyone have any ideas?

I do think that perhaps dogs and cats should be made harder to tame
for Convicts if they can tame rats.  Maybe only a tripe ration would
do the trick in this case?



